<title>RUSSIA: TENNIS-INJURY PUTS KAFELNIKOV OUT OF U.S. OPEN.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-INJURY PUTS KAFELNIKOV OUT OF U.S. OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-08-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Open champion Yevgeny Kafelnikov of Russia will miss the U.S. Open after pulling a muscle in his back while playing golf, his trainer said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Anatoly Lepeshin told Itar-Tass news agency the world number four had returned to Moscow on his doctor's advice after a final training session in New York on Saturday.</p>
<p>The championships begin on Monday.</p>
</text>
